cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
title: "Between the Model and the Shell: Deterministic Runtime Governance for Probabilistic Software Engineering Agents"
abstract: >-
  TBound is a Linux supervisor that mediates the read, write, edit and bash tool
  calls of the Pi coding agent. It enforces a fixed policy, runs bash in an
  isolated rootless Podman cell, publishes changes to the repository only when the
  policy allows them, and records decisions and effects in durable journals. It is
  the artifact of a master thesis on policy enforcement and over-refusal for coding
  agents.
authors:
